# Phase 13: Admin Panel Completed

I've successfully finalized Phase 13, bringing together the platform's core administrative capabilities into a unified Admin Dashboard.

## Changes Made
- **Backend Simulation Controls**: Updated the `telemetrySimulator` to maintain state, allowing dynamic starting, stopping, and scaling of the simulation loop interval.
- **Admin API**: Added a new set of API endpoints (`/api/admin/simulation/*`) for administrators to control the simulation logic securely.
- **Unified Admin Dashboard**: Replaced the standalone User Management view with a master `AdminDashboard` component at `/admin`. This view aligns perfectly with the provided `admin dashbord.png` design.
  - **KPI Header**: Shows top-level system summaries.
  - **User Directory**: Retained the table to assign roles and suspend accounts.
  - **Simulation Control**: A new panel displaying real-time simulation status, allowing admins to pause/play the telemetry engine and alter the speed (e.g. 1x to 5x intervals).
  - **Activity Timeline**: A minimal timeline of recent platform audits integrated directly onto the dashboard.
- **Routing & Navigation**: Streamlined the sidebar so "Admin Console" correctly routes to the new, unified view.

## Verification
- I've verified that the frontend layout accurately mirrors the dark, neon-accented Admin Dashboard mockup.
- The `adminService.js` flawlessly interfaces with the backend to handle simulation triggers.
- The dashboard ensures you can now slow down or entirely halt incoming telemetry, which will be essential when testing alert thresholds manually!

